  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Evaluate $\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/3)).$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/3))=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The definition of $\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{x}+{e}^{-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/3)) & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/3)}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1/3)}+{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{3}+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1+9}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
